  "memories": [
    {
      "content": "# Event Finder — My Event Preferences\n\n_Edit freely. `/find` reads this when the search is an EVENT (gig, match, show, festival, conference). Leave a line blank to ignore it._\n\n## Region & currency\n- Country / region: \n- Currency: \n- Willing to travel: \n\n## Dates\n- Date flexibility: (specific date | any date on tour | weekends only | date range)\n- Earliest / latest acceptable date: \n\n## Budget & tickets\n- Max price per ticket (all-in, incl. fees): \n- Number of tickets: \n- Seating preference: (standing | seated | best available | specific section)\n- Together/adjacent seats required: yes\n\n## Seller legitimacy (important for tickets)\n- Prefer PRIMARY / official sellers only (Ticketmaster, AXS, See Tickets, venue box office, official promoter): yes\n- Allow verified resale (Twickets, Ticketmaster resale, AXS official resale) at/near face value: yes\n- Block secondary touts / above-face resale (Viagogo, StubHub markups): yes\n- Always verify seller is official/authorised and warn on any resale premium: yes\n\n## Availability verification\n- Confirm tickets are really available (reach seat-selection / basket), not just \"on sale\" label: yes\n- Note on-sale date + presale codes if event not yet on general sale: yes\n\n## Follow-up / notifications\n- If sold out or not yet on sale, offer to watch and notify (on-sale date, presale, resale drops): yes\n- Add a calendar entry for on-sale date / event date: ask me\n\n## Notes / taste\n- (Free text — accessibility needs, preferred artists/teams, no-go venues, etc.)\n",
      "path": "event-finder/event-preferences.md"
    },
    {
      "content": "# Product Finder — My Search Preferences\n\n_Edit freely. `/find` reads this before every search and applies it. Leave a line blank or delete it to ignore that preference._\n\n## Region & currency\n- Country / region: \n- Currency: \n- Deliver to (postcode, optional, for stock checks): \n\n## Budget\n- Default max budget: (leave blank = no cap)\n- Flag anything over RRP as a warning: yes\n\n## Condition\n- Accept used / open-box / refurbished? no (new only) — change to \"yes\" to include\n- If used accepted, minimum condition: \n\n## Legitimacy / trust (for unknown sellers)\n- Run legitimacy check on sellers I don't recognise: yes\n- Checks to run: Trustpilot rating + review count, Companies House registration, physical store presence, authorised-dealer status\n- Minimum Trustpilot score to recommend: 4.0\n- Prefer authorised dealers over marketplaces/resellers: yes\n\n## Retailers\n- Preferred retailers (try first): \n- Blocked retailers (never suggest): \n\n## Stock verification\n- Require real stock proof (add-to-basket / checkout), not just \"in stock\" label: yes\n- Include in-store-only stock in results: yes (mark clearly)\n\n## Multiple products\n- When I ask for several items, prefer: one seller for all (fewer deliveries) | cheapest per item — choose: cheapest per item\n- Show a combined total when multi-item: yes\n\n## Delivery\n- Priority: (cheapest | fastest | free) — choose: free then fastest\n- Max acceptable delivery time: \n\n## Follow-up\n- After a search, default next step I usually want: (deeper stock verify | price watch | checkout prep | nothing) — choose: ask me\n\n## Notes / taste\n- (Free text — anything else the searcher should know about how I shop.)\n",
      "path": "product-finder/search-preferences.md"
    },
    {
      "content": "# Product & Event Finder\n\n**Type:** tracker\n\nGeneric product/event search app. User names a product (or event); the app finds where to get it, verifies real availability by browsing, checks seller legitimacy, and prepares checkout — never paying on the user's behalf.\n\n## Workflow (3 skills)\n- `/search-setup` — one-time: verify browsing/Playwright tooling, create the preferences file if missing, kick off first search.\n- `/find <product|event>` — main flow: clarify → search → browser-verify real stock → legitimacy-check unknown sellers → populate a tracker → follow up.\n- `/checkout` — prepare a chosen purchase up to the login/payment step, then hand to the user.\n\n## Files\n- Preferences (non-pupa-standard) live BESIDE this folder, one per search kind:\n  - `product-finder/search-preferences.md` — physical products.\n  - `event-finder/event-preferences.md` — events (gigs, matches, shows, festivals, conferences).\n  `/find` detects product vs event and reads the matching file at the start.\n- Pupa-standard files (skills, this AGENTS.md) stay under `pupa/`.\n- One search = one tracker, named after the item (keeps history, keeps searches separate). Fields: seller, price, status, delivery, trust, link. Add an `image` field when the item has a representative picture (product photo, event/exhibition hero) — fill it with the real image URL pulled from the source page, never a placeholder.\n- After a search, offer to keep the user updated: ask if they want notifications about stock/price/on-sale changes. If yes, schedule a recurring re-check that re-verifies and notifies on change. User can also attach extra components (calendar for restock/event/reminder dates, more fields) around a search.\n\n## Hard guardrails\n- **Availability = proven, not labelled.** An \"add to basket\" button or \"in stock\" text is not proof. Confirm via real checkout/basket/fulfilment check. If automation is blocked (bot protection), say \"displayed in stock, unconfirmed\" — never claim verified.\n- **Legitimacy.** Legitimacy-check sellers the user wouldn't recognise: Trustpilot (live, via browser — it blocks plain fetch), Companies House, physical presence, authorised-dealer vs reseller/marketplace. Cite sources.\n- **Privacy / credentials.** NEVER enter or request the user's login, address, or payment details. NEVER place an order for them. `/checkout` stops at the credential/payment boundary and hands off. Postcode only for stock checks, only if volunteered.\n- **Browser conduct.** Answer cookie banners with their own accept/reject buttons — never delete consent elements or evade bot protection. Blocked means report it unverified, not route around it. Resolve pasted links by opening them and reading the true title.\n",
      "path": "pupa/AGENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "content": "---\ndescription: Skills, subagents and multi-agent slack rooms\nwhen_to_use: when creating skills or subagents, using /commands, or working with slack rooms\nversion: 20\n---\n- **Skills** — reusable playbooks that double as `/commands` in chat.\n  Each app has its own set (this guide is one). Ask the agent to create\n  one, or write it yourself in the memory tree under `pupa/skills/`.\n- **Subagents** — named delegates with their own persona and\n  instructions. The main agent creates them and hands off focused tasks.\n- **Orchestrator** — the top-level agent: creates and manages myapps and\n  delegates work to each app's agent.\n\n**Slack rooms.** A component with channels, group DMs and DMs. The\nworkspace roster is simply *all* the myapp's subagents — creating a\nsubagent adds it to the roster; nothing lives in the component but rooms\nand their transcripts. @-mention an agent (or post in its DM) to wake it:\nit reads the channel's history for context, works with the app's tools,\nand posts its reply back to the channel. Agents can @-mention each other,\nso one message can start a chain of replies. Exporting the app keeps the\nchannels and the agent personas but strips the transcripts.",
      "path": "pupa/plugins/pupa-guide/skills/pupa-agents/SKILL.md"
    },
    {
      "content": "---\ndescription: React to canvas events (an item moved) by proposing a chat — the pupa/automations.json rule format and its guards\nwhen_to_use: when the user wants the app to act automatically on a canvas change, or when authoring or editing automation rules\nversion: 20\n---\nAn **automation** reacts *inside* a myapp to a canvas event by proposing a\nchat. Declarative config, no code — rules ride the `.pupa` bundle and only\never start a model turn, always behind a confirm bubble unless a rule\nexplicitly opts out.\n\n**Trigger (v1).** `item.moved` — a user changes any **select** field on a\ntracker item: dragging a kanban lane, editing the field on the card, or\nsaving the edit sheet. Independent of the board's group-by — a rule\nwatching `Priority` fires while the board is grouped by `Status`, and in\ngrid view too. One event per changed select field. Agent moves never\ntrigger (so a reaction can't loop on itself).\n\n**Where.** One file per app: `pupa/automations.json`. Shape mirrors Claude\nCode hook config — an `automations` map keyed by event name, each a list of\nrules — but these are Pupa domain events, not harness hooks.\n\n```json\n{\"automations\":{\"item.moved\":[\n  {\"id\":\"review-on-move\",\n   \"matcher\":{\"field\":\"Status\",\"toColumn\":\"Review\"},\n   \"action\":{\"startThread\":{\"prompt\":\"Review {{item.title}}.\"}},\n   \"confirm\":true}\n]}}\n```\n\n**Fields.**\n- `id` (required) — unique per rule; also the lock key.\n- `matcher` — field-equality predicates, **all must hold (AND)**; omit or\n  `{}` to match every move. Keys are any of the item's own fields plus the\n  transition keys `field` / `toColumn` / `fromColumn`. Add `field` whenever\n  two select fields share an option name, or the rule fires on both.\n- `action.startThread.prompt` (required) — the chat prompt. Templates:\n  `{{item.title}}`, `{{item.<field>}}`, `{{field}}`, `{{toColumn}}`,\n  `{{fromColumn}}`, substituted literally (no code).\n- `confirm` — `true` (default) proposes a Start/Dismiss bubble; `false`\n  auto-fires with no prompt. Only ship `confirm:false` in bundles you\n  trust — it invokes the model on a plain canvas move.\n\n**Guards (automatic — you don't configure them).**\n- **Self-mutation** — the reaction's own edits don't re-trigger the rule.\n- **Once-per-transition** — the same move fires once within a short window.\n- **In-flight lock** — while a rule's reaction for an item is running, the\n  same item won't re-fire it (a timeout backstop frees a stuck one).\n\n**Limits.** v1 has one event (`item.moved`), one action (`startThread`),\nequality-only matching, and no chaining. A malformed rule is skipped, not\nfatal — the rest of the file still loads.",
      "path": "pupa/plugins/pupa-guide/skills/pupa-automations/SKILL.md"
    },
    {
      "content": "---\ndescription: The component shapes a myapp canvas can hold and how they combine\nwhen_to_use: when choosing, combining or linking components, or asked what shapes exist\nversion: 20\n---\nA myapp's canvas holds components. Available shapes:\n\n- **calculator** — live numeric model with tunable inputs + formula rows\n- **calendar** — time-indexed events in a list or month grid\n- **chart** — pie/bar/line visualisation of tracker or calculator data\n- **checklist** — simple done/not-done items, no per-row fields\n- **slack** — multi-agent chat rooms (subagent personas, channels, @-mentions)\n- **tracker** — multi-field records in a table/kanban (fields, filters, cards)\n\n**Combining.** One myapp mixes shapes freely. Items link across\ncomponents — a tracker row to a calendar event, a task to a parent\nrecord. Calculators and charts read live from other components, and a\nchart can be embedded straight into chat.\n\n**Views, not shapes.** Kanban is a tracker view mode (table ⇄ cards),\nnot a separate component.\n\n**Finding and scanning.** Both tracker views have a search box above\nthe cards — it matches any field, including link URLs, and in kanban it\nnarrows the cards without dropping columns. The shrink button next to\nthe view toggle collapses every card to its title for a whole-board\nview; it sticks per component. Cards with several links show the first\nfew and a \"+N\" you can tap to see the rest.",
      "path": "pupa/plugins/pupa-guide/skills/pupa-components/SKILL.md"
    },
    {
      "content": "---\ndescription: How Pupa remembers: memories, sessions, change history, archive\nwhen_to_use: when asked what persists, how to undo changes, or how to hide an app\nversion: 20\n---\n- **Memories** — a filesystem-like tree of notes and folders that lives\n  *inside* the app, not on the device's file system. Notes are markdown\n  (`.md`); config notes can be `.json` and show verbatim as code, so\n  indentation survives. Browse and edit it from the Memories tab; the agent\n  reads and writes it too. Persists across sessions.\n- **Sessions** — \"New session\" starts a fresh conversation. The canvas\n  and memories stay. Past conversations are kept on-device and re-open with\n  their full history when you reopen the app — even after a long time away.\n- **History** — every canvas change is recorded per myapp. Browse the\n  History tab and restore any earlier state in one tap. Tap **Take\n  snapshot** to pin the current state permanently (kept forever); pinned\n  snapshots can be **Export**ed as a `.pupa` file (same share screen as\n  Settings, flagged as the pinned version). Pins survive deleting\n  the myapp — find them all in **Settings ▸ Pinned snapshots**, where a\n  deleted app can be restored (revived) from a pin.\n- **Archive** — hide a myapp without deleting it (its data and memories\n  are kept). Browse, restore or delete from Settings ▸ Archive.\n- **Recently deleted** — deleting a myapp is undoable for 180 days.\n  Settings ▸ Recently deleted lists them (including ones deleted on another\n  device, and ones a sync removed on its own) and restores the last saved\n  state — chats, components, and any skills or subagents a sync took with\n  it. Dismissing the \"Sync removed …\"\n  banner loses nothing — the app waits here. Each row can also be **deleted\n  permanently** — that erases its saved state, pinned snapshots included, on\n  every device.\n- **Recovering lost skills** — if a sync takes a skill or subagent from a\n  myapp that is still here, a \"Sync removed N memory files\" banner offers to\n  put them back. Recoverable for 30 days.",
      "path": "pupa/plugins/pupa-guide/skills/pupa-memory/SKILL.md"
    },
    {
      "content": "---\ndescription: Share and install myapps as .pupa files\nwhen_to_use: when exporting, sharing, importing or installing an app\nversion: 20\n---\nA `.pupa` file is an inert snapshot of a myapp: its components, optionally\nyour records and memories, plus the app's agent instructions and skills.\nNo code runs from the file itself.\n\n**Export.** Settings ▸ Import & Export: pick components, choose whether\nrecords and memories ride along, then Share (AirDrop, Messages, Files…) —\non Mac, Save, which writes the `.pupa` wherever you choose.\nExporting a pinned snapshot (from History or Settings ▸ Pinned snapshots)\nopens this same screen with a \"Pinned version\" banner — records and memories\ndefault off there too.\n\n**Install.** Open a `.pupa` file (or import from Settings). A confirmation\nsheet shows what's inside before anything is added. Imported agent\ninstructions run with your tools once installed — only install bundles\nyou trust.\n\n**Marketplace.** Settings ▸ Import & Export ▸ Import an app links out to\npupa-app.com/marketplace. Installing from there sends the app back to Pupa\nthrough the same confirmation sheet.",
      "path": "pupa/plugins/pupa-guide/skills/pupa-sharing/SKILL.md"
    },
    {
      "content": "---\ndescription: Where things live: the on-device app vs the backend, and standing instructions\nwhen_to_use: when unsure whether something belongs in the app or the backend, which skill system you're touching, or how to change standing behaviour\nversion: 20\n---\n**App vs backend.** Everything the user sees — components and their\nitems, memories, skills, `AGENTS.md` — is app state, created and edited\n**on the user's device** through the app's own tools. The backend only\nruns the model plus a few server-side tools (web search, shell, …) and\nstores **no app data**. Never write app content to a backend path or via\na shell unless explicitly told to; if unsure where something belongs, ask.\n\n**Canvas vs memory.** Components hold data items; memory is a *separate*\nper-app markdown note tree for durable context — not canvas data. Two\ndifferent stores; don't cross them. Memory paths are an in-app structure,\nnot host file paths — never reach for it via a shell.\n\n**Two skill systems.** *App* skills are on-device `SKILL.md` files —\nyours under `pupa/skills/<name>/`, bundled ones under\n`pupa/plugins/<plugin>/skills/<name>/` (this guide is one). A backend may\nseparately expose its own read-only skills library. App skills are\nalways the on-device files.\n\n**Standing behaviour.** Persistent instructions for an app's main agent\nlive at `pupa/AGENTS.md` (subagents: `pupa/agents/<name>/AGENTS.md`).\nEdit those to change behaviour permanently — not memory, not a skill.",
      "path": "pupa/plugins/pupa-guide/skills/pupa-system/SKILL.md"
    },
    {
      "content": "---\ndescription: What Pupa is and what it can do — guide entry point\nwhen_to_use: when the user asks what Pupa is, what it can do, or how its pieces fit together\nversion: 20\n---\nPupa builds apps around you: describe what you need in chat and the agent\nassembles a **myapp** — a canvas of components it edits live while you talk.\n\n**Boundaries — who is what**\n- **Orchestrator** — the top-level chat. Creates, renames, archives and\n  deletes myapps and delegates work to their agents. Has its own memories\n  and skills; no canvas of its own.\n- **Myapp** — one workspace: its own agent, canvas, memories, skills and\n  subagents.\n- **Component** — one shape on a myapp's canvas (tracker, calendar, …).\n- **Item** — one record inside a component (row, event, task…).\n- **Memories** — each myapp (and the orchestrator) keeps its own\n  filesystem-like tree of markdown notes and folders living *inside* the\n  app — not on the device's file system. Edited by you and the agent\n  alike; persists across sessions. Durable context, not records.\n\nItems can link across components *within one myapp*. Myapps don't share\ndata — an app moves between devices or people as a `.pupa` file.\n\n**Go deeper** (users: type the `/command`; agents: `app_skill_view`)\n- /pupa-components — the shapes a canvas can hold and how they combine\n- /pupa-sharing — export and install myapps as `.pupa` files\n- /pupa-memory — memories, sessions, change history, archive\n- /pupa-agents — skills, subagents and slack rooms\n- /pupa-automations — react to canvas events (an item moved) by proposing a chat\n- /pupa-system — where things live: on-device app vs backend, standing instructions",
      "path": "pupa/plugins/pupa-guide/skills/pupa/SKILL.md"
    },
    {
      "content": "---\ndescription: Prepare a chosen item's checkout up to (but not through) the login/payment step, so the user can finish the purchase themselves. Never enters credentials or payment details.\nwhen_to_use: When the user picks a seller/item from a search and says \"check out\", \"buy this\", \"get it ready\", or \"prepare the purchase\".\n---\n\n# Product & Event Finder — Checkout Prep\n\nDrive the browser to get a purchase ready, then STOP and hand control to the user at the credential/payment boundary. You prepare; the human pays.\n\n## 1. Confirm the target\n- Which item + which seller (from the tracker). Confirm variant, price, and quantity with the user before touching the site.\n- Re-open the product page and re-verify it's still in stock (stock moves fast). If gone, tell the user and offer the next-best seller from the tracker.\n\n## 2. Build the basket\n- Add the correct item/variant/qty to the basket. Handle cookie banners as in `/find` — their own buttons only, never a consent or bot-protection bypass.\n- Open the basket/cart and confirm: right product, right price, right quantity. Report the subtotal.\n\n## 3. Advance to the checkout boundary\n- Proceed toward checkout until you reach the point where the site asks to sign in, or to enter personal/delivery/payment details.\n- STOP there. Do not create an account, sign in, enter email/address, or enter any payment/card details.\n- Note anything the user should decide: delivery option + cost, click-and-collect vs delivery, any surcharge, cut-off time for next-day.\n\n## 4. Hand off\n- Tell the user exactly where they are (\"basket ready, £X subtotal, stopped at sign-in/payment\") and what's left for them to do.\n- If they're on their own device, hand the open page over. Do NOT ask them to share passwords or card numbers with you.\n\n## Guardrails (hard rules)\n- NEVER enter, request, or store credentials, personal details, or payment information. This is a firm boundary — if the flow demands them, stop and pass to the user.\n- NEVER complete a purchase / place an order on the user's behalf.\n- Keep the user's data in their hands; you only prepare the page.\n- If unsure whether a step crosses the line, stop and ask.\n",
      "path": "pupa/skills/checkout/SKILL.md"
    },
    {
      "content": "---\ndescription: Search for any product or event the user wants, verify real availability by browsing, legitimacy-check unknown sellers, and populate a tracker with the findings.\nwhen_to_use: When the user wants to find/buy a product or get tickets for an event — e.g. \"find me X\", \"where can I buy Y\", \"is Z in stock\", \"tickets for ...\".\n---\n\n# Product & Event Finder — Find\n\nTurn a product/event request into a verified, trustworthy shortlist in a tracker.\n\n## 0. Load context\n- Decide PRODUCT vs EVENT from the request (a gig, match, show, festival, conference, \"tickets for…\" = event; a physical item = product).\n- Product → read `product-finder/search-preferences.md`. Event → read `event-finder/event-preferences.md`. Both live beside `pupa/`.\n- Apply the relevant prefs (region, budget, legitimacy strictness, blocked sellers, delivery/date rules, notifications). If the file is missing, run `/search-setup` first.\n\n## 1. Understand the request\n- Identify the exact item: model/variant/colour/edition, or event + date + location. Resolve any link the user pastes by opening it and reading the real title.\n- If ambiguous or missing key facts, ASK (batch the questions): which variant, budget, new vs used, region/postcode, urgency. Don't guess on things that change the result.\n\n## 2. Search wide\n- Web search for retailers/sellers carrying the item in the user's region. Gather candidates.\n- Respect blocked retailers; put preferred retailers first.\n\n## 3. Verify real availability (do NOT trust labels)\n- Open each candidate's product page in the browser.\n- An active \"add to basket\" / \"in stock\" label is NOT proof. Confirm by actually pushing through: add to basket / start checkout / run the retailer's stock/fulfilment check (e.g. postcode delivery check). A page can show \"add to trolley\" yet be out of stock at checkout.\n- Cookie banners: answer them with the banner's own accept/reject buttons. Never delete consent elements, and never work around bot protection (CAPTCHA, Cloudflare) — a wall you can't pass legitimately is a hard stop, not a puzzle.\n- If you filled a basket purely to test stock, empty it again before leaving the site.\n- Record the true state: in stock online (checkout-verified), ships-in-N-days, in-store only (+ which store / qty), or out of stock. If automation is blocked (e.g. Amazon bot protection), say so honestly — \"displayed in stock, couldn't confirm via checkout\" — don't claim verified.\n\n## 4. Legitimacy check (unknown sellers)\n- For any seller the user wouldn't obviously recognise, and per the prefs strictness:\n  - Trustpilot: live score + review count (browser — Trustpilot blocks plain fetch; navigate + read).\n  - Companies House: registered company name + number + incorporation year + active status.\n  - Physical store presence, authorised-dealer status, marketplace-vs-direct seller.\n- Flag resellers / marketplace \"warehouse/used\" listings clearly.\n\n## 5. Populate a tracker\n- Create ONE new tracker per search (one search = one tracker), named after the item. Keeps history and keeps searches separate.\n- Product fields: seller, price, status (select: In stock online / In stock ships 3-5d / In-store only / Awaiting stock / Out of stock), delivery (notes incl. verification result), trust (legitimacy proof), link.\n- Event fields: seller/platform, price (per ticket, all-in), status (select: On sale / Presale / Sold out / Resale only / Not yet on sale), date + venue, seats/section, trust (primary vs resale, any over-face premium), link.\n- For events, prefer official/primary sellers; clearly flag secondary/resale and any above-face markup per prefs. Verify by reaching seat-selection/basket, not just an \"on sale\" label.\n- **Images (if appropriate).** When an item has a representative picture — a product photo, or an event/exhibition/gig hero — add an `image` field and populate each row with the REAL image URL taken from the source page (the page's `og:image` meta or its main hero `<img>`). One image per row; never invent, guess, or placeholder a URL — skip the image when the source has none.\n- Add only sellers with genuine or plausible stock; note excluded backorder/out-of-stock ones in the summary. Set the tracker `summary` with date + headline findings.\n\n## 6. Follow up\n- Give a short ranked recommendation (best stock + trust first).\n- **Ask if they want to be notified / kept updated** about this search — e.g. stock coming back, price drops, event on-sale date. If yes, set it up: schedule a recurring re-check that re-runs the verification and sends a notification on change. Confirm cadence with the user.\n- Offer other add-ons for tracking this search over time: a calendar component (e.g. event date, restock/launch date, price-check reminders), or extra tracker fields. One search = one tracker, but the user can attach more components around it.\n- Offer next steps per prefs: deeper stock verify, price watch, or `/checkout` to prep a purchase. Ask which.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Respect each site's terms and consent choices: no consent bypass, no bot-protection evasion, no automated ordering. If a site blocks automation, report it unverified and move on.\n- Cite sources (product pages, Trustpilot, Companies House) so claims are checkable.\n- Never enter user credentials, address, or payment info during verification.\n",
      "path": "pupa/skills/find/SKILL.md"
    },
    {
      "content": "---\ndescription: One-time setup for the Product Finder app — verifies browsing/Playwright tooling works, creates the search-preferences file if missing, and kicks off the first search.\nwhen_to_use: When the user first opens this app, says \"set up\", \"get started\", or when /find reports tooling or preferences are missing.\n---\n\n# Product & Event Finder — Setup\n\nGoal: confirm the app can actually search, make sure a preferences file exists, then hand off to `/find`.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. **Check tooling.**\n   - Confirm browser + Playwright tools are available (browser_navigate, browser_click, browser_snapshot, etc.) and web search.\n   - Smoke test: navigate to a simple page (e.g. https://example.com) and read the title. If it fails, tell the user browsing isn't available and stop — the app needs it.\n   - Note that cookie banners are answered with their own buttons, and a bot wall is a hard stop (see /find).\n\n2. **Preferences files.**\n   - Two preference files live beside the `pupa/` folder (at memories root — NOT inside pupa/):\n     - `product-finder/search-preferences.md` — for physical products.\n     - `event-finder/event-preferences.md` — for events (gigs, matches, shows, festivals).\n   - If either is missing, create it from the template shipped with this app (product: region, budget, condition, legitimacy, retailers, delivery, follow-up; event: region, dates, ticket budget, seating, primary-vs-resale legitimacy, notifications).\n   - If present, read and briefly reflect back the key settings so the user can confirm/adjust.\n\n3. **Ask what they want.**\n   - \"Anything you're looking for right now, or just setting up?\"\n   - If they name a product/event → invoke `/find` with it.\n   - If not → tell them they can run `/find <product>` any time, and edit `product-finder/search-preferences.md` to tune taste.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Never write personal data (addresses, card, logins) into the preferences file. Postcode for stock checks only, and only if the user volunteers it.\n- Keep pupa-standard files in `pupa/`; keep app data/preferences in the `product-finder/` folder beside it.\n",
      "path": "pupa/skills/search-setup/SKILL.md"
    },
    {
      "content": "---\ndescription: Record durable, app-level learnings from this conversation to pupa/MEMORIES.md\nwhen_to_use: when the user runs /to-memory or asks to capture what was learned this session\n---\nCapture what would help next time someone works on *this* app — especially\npoints where the user redirected you or an initial approach needed realignment.\n\n1. Re-read this conversation. Extract *general, durable* guidance: conventions\n   clarified, preferences stated, gotchas, and anything that needed\n   realignment mid-task. Skip one-off task specifics.\n2. Read the existing `pupa/MEMORIES.md` (if present) so you merge, not duplicate.\n3. Write to `pupa/MEMORIES.md` or your AGENTS.md file with the merged result — short bullets under clear\n   headings, the new insight integrated in place. Choose AGENTS.md for info you should always be aware of in every conversation, \n   while choose MEMORIES.md for info that is not always needed.\n4. Tell the user in one line what you added.",
      "path": "pupa/skills/to-memory/SKILL.md"
    }
